/P 135 0 R
/T (With the semiconductor and components hubs situated in the region, many Asian economies have experienced remarkable growth in AI hardware exports. These exports increased sharply after 2016, reaching more than USD 1 trillion by 2025. Export growth has been concentrated in economies embedded in the regional hardware ecosystem, particularly China, South Korea, Hong Kong, Singapore and Malaysia. )
/E (With the semiconductor and components hubs situated in the region, many Asian economies have experienced remarkable growth in AI hardware exports. These exports increased sharply after 2016, reaching more than USD 1 trillion by 2025. Export growth has been concentrated in economies embedded in the regional hardware ecosystem, particularly China, South Korea, Hong Kong, Singapore and Malaysia. )
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
492 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 135 0 R
/T (For Singapore, this points to a dual role in the AI economy: not only is local demand for AI-related skills accelerating, as shown by the Jobstreet AI Gauge, but Singapore sits within one of the hubs supplying the physical hardware that powers AI systems globally. This suggests that the AI boom is benefiting hardware-linked economies disproportionately, while others have seen more limited gains. )
/E (For Singapore, this points to a dual role in the AI economy: not only is local demand for AI-related skills accelerating, as shown by the Jobstreet AI Gauge, but Singapore sits within one of the hubs supplying the physical hardware that powers AI systems globally. This suggests that the AI boom is benefiting hardware-linked economies disproportionately, while others have seen more limited gains. )
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [1]
>>
